    },
    {
      "name": "Ranking Row",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "Code-led result card; the top pick adds a 2px orange border and the Best match chip.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-row\"><div class=\"ds-row-head\"><span class=\"ds-rank\">1</span><span class=\"ds-iata\">IST</span><div class=\"ds-row-city\"><b>Istanbul</b><small>Türkiye · history, food</small></div><div class=\"ds-row-price\"><span>$986</span><small>each, est.</small></div></div><div class=\"ds-split\"><i style=\"flex:2;background:#2F5BEA\"></i><i style=\"flex:4;background:#0B7A6E\"></i><i style=\"flex:5;background:#E5A000\"></i></div><div class=\"ds-row-meta\"><small>$2,959 total · 70% even</small><span class=\"ds-chip-a\">Best match</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-row{width:360px;padding:16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;background:#fff;border:2px solid #FF5A1F;border-radius:12px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(17,20,24,.06),0 4px 14px rgba(17,20,24,.06);font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#111418;transition:transform .16s}.ds-row:active{transform:scale(.985)}.ds-row-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}.ds-rank{width:20px;font:700 20px/22px 'Sofia Sans Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;color:#59616C}.ds-iata{min-width:58px;font:800 32px/32px 'Sofia Sans Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.4px}.ds-row-city{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;font-size:15px}.ds-row small{font-size:13px;color:#59616C}.ds-row-price{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end}.ds-row-price span{font:700 26px/28px 'Sofia Sans Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-row-price small{font-size:12px}.ds-split{display:flex;gap:2px;height:4px}.ds-split i{border-radius:1px}.ds-row-meta{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center}.ds-chip-a{padding:4px 10px;border-radius:999px;background:#FF5A1F;color:#111418;font:500 12px/16px Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Boarding Pass",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "boarding-pass-carrier",
      "description": "Signature: one pass per friend, livery band, code-to-code route, ruled fields, perforated stub with the total.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-pass\"><div class=\"ds-carrier\"><span>GoTogether · Boarding pass</span><span>1 of 3</span></div><div class=\"ds-band\"></div><div class=\"ds-pbody\"><div class=\"ds-holder\"><span class=\"ds-av\">MA</span><b>Maya</b></div><div class=\"ds-route\"><div><span class=\"ds-f\">From</span><span class=\"ds-code\">LON</span><small>London</small></div><div class=\"ds-track\"><i></i><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2F5BEA\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"><path d=\"M10 18l2-6-6-1-2 2-2-1 2-3-2-3 2-1 2 2 6-1-2-6 2-1 5 7h4a1.5 1.5 0 010 3h-4l-5 7z\"/></svg><i></i></div><div class=\"r\"><span class=\"ds-f\">To</span><span class=\"ds-code\">IST</span><small>Istanbul</small></div></div><div class=\"ds-fields\"><div><span class=\"ds-f\">Flight</span><b>4 h</b></div><div><span class=\"ds-f\">Nights</span><b>3</b></div><div style=\"flex:1\"><span class=\"ds-f\">Dates</span><b>Fri 11 Dec – Mon 14 Dec</b></div></div></div><div class=\"ds-perf\"></div><div class=\"ds-stub\"><div><span class=\"ds-f\">Pays · estimate</span><small>Flight, room share, food</small></div><span class=\"ds-total\">$577</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-pass{width:360px;background:#fff;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(17,20,24,.06),0 4px 14px rgba(17,20,24,.06);font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#111418;position:relative;transition:transform .16s}.ds-pass:active{transform:scale(.985)}.ds-carrier{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:8px 16px;background:#111418;color:#fff;font:600 10.5px/13px Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.8px;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-band{height:4px;background:#2F5BEA}.ds-pbody{padding:16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}.ds-holder{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:15px}.ds-av{width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;background:#2F5BEA;color:#fff;font:600 10px/26px Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:center}.ds-route{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}.ds-route>div:not(.ds-track){display:flex;flex-direction:column}.ds-route .r{align-items:flex-end}.ds-f{font:600 10.5px/13px Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.8px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#59616C}.ds-code{font:800 32px/32px 'Sofia Sans Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.4px}.ds-route small,.ds-stub small{font:500 12px/16px Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#59616C}.ds-track{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;padding-top:8px}.ds-track i{flex:1;height:2px;background:#2F5BEA;opacity:.6}.ds-fields{display:flex;border-top:1px solid #D5DAE0;border-bottom:1px solid #D5DAE0}.ds-fields>div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;padding:8px;font-size:13px}.ds-fields>div+div{border-left:1px solid #D5DAE0}.ds-perf{height:18px;margin:0 17px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#AEB5BE 7px,transparent 7px) 0 50%/12px 1.5px repeat-x;position:relative}.ds-perf::before,.ds-perf::after{content:'';position:absolute;top:0;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:#E7EAEE}.ds-perf::before{left:-26px}.ds-perf::after{right:-26px}.ds-stub{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:8px 16px 16px}.ds-stub>div{display:flex;flex-direction:column}.ds-total{font:800 40px/40px 'Sofia Sans Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Header Icon Button",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "header-icon-button",
      "description": "44pt circular stock button for back, share and edit in the floating header.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-hbtn\" aria-label=\"Back\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M15 18l-6-6 6-6\"/></svg></button>",
      "css": ".ds-hbtn{width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#fff;border:1px solid #D5DAE0;color:#111418;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .16s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)}.ds-hbtn:active{transform:scale(.97);opacity:.9}.ds-hbtn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #FF5A1F;outline-offset:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Departure Board",
    "overview": "GoTogether is printed travel stock laid out on an airport-grey concourse. Every surface is a piece of white pass stock with square shoulders; every friend in a trip is a livery colour that follows them from avatar to route arc to the band across the top of their pass. The app's one loud colour, signal orange, marks the place everyone lands: the best match, the selected mode, the primary action, the meeting point on the map. Everything else is near-black ink and cool greys.\n\nThe voice is the pass's own. A condensed bold grotesk (Sofia Sans Condensed, 700 and 800) sets three-letter airport codes, city names, trip names and prices; the platform sans carries all reading text. Ranking rows lead with the IATA code the way a departure board does, and the per-person breakdown is a literal stack of boarding passes with a perforated stub holding what each friend pays. Density is moderate: one 640 px column on phones, a two-column working layout from 1024 px.\n\nDark mode is the same system under cabin lights, not a different mood: the ground goes to near-black navy, stock to a lifted slate, orange warms a step to stay vivid. The world explicitly rejects hero-photo destination cards and the cream-and-serif editorial look it replaced.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Airport-grey ground, white pass stock, near-black ink; one signal orange.",
      "A fixed livery colour per traveler, carried through every mark that represents them.",
      "Condensed bold grotesk for codes, names and figures; platform sans for everything else; tabular figures on every price.",
      "Square-shouldered 12 px stock; perforations and punched notches on passes.",
      "One elevation per card: soft shadow in light, hairline edge in dark.",
      "Springs for anything that moves under the finger; a single motion set app-wide."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Signal Rule",
        "body": "Signal orange marks only where the group lands or what is selected: best match, selected mode, primary path, the meeting point. It is a fill and a graphic colour; it never sets text on stock.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Livery Rule",
        "body": "A traveler's colour is fixed by their position in the trip and appears on every mark that stands for them, and only on those. Cost categories use the neutral ramp, never a livery.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Code-Led Rule",
        "body": "A city in a list is introduced by its three-letter code in the condensed face before its name, as on a departure board.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Field Rule",
        "body": "Tracked uppercase exists only as data labels printed on a boarding pass, sitting directly over the value they name. Everywhere else labels are sentence case; never set tracked caps above a heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every price, rank and figure uses tabular numerals so columns of money line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Elevation Rule",
        "body": "A card is lifted once: shadow in light, hairline in dark, never both, and never a second shadow on something inside it.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Perforation Rule",
        "body": "What a person pays sits on a stub torn off below (or beside) a dashed perforation with punched notches; the stub is the only place a pass shows its total.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep signal orange to the best match, the selected state, the primary action and the meeting point; put ink, not white, on it.",
      "Do give every traveler one livery colour by trip position and repeat it on their avatar, band, route, map arc and split segment.",
      "Do lead city rows and pass endpoints with the three-letter code in the condensed face.",
      "Do set every price in tabular figures and label every figure as an estimate (\"each, est.\", \"Pays · estimate\").",
      "Do lift a card once: Stock shadow in light, hairline in dark.",
      "Do use the shared motion set: snappy spring for press and toggles, glide spring for things changing place, 160 / 280 / 520 ms with cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1), 45 ms stagger.",
      "Do keep touch targets at 44 pt and text at 4.5:1 or better in both themes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't set tracked uppercase outside a boarding pass's printed fields, and never as an eyebrow over a heading.",
      "Don't use a livery colour for cost categories, status or decoration; the breakdown ramp stays neutral.",
      "Don't use hero photography for destinations; a city is its code, name, flag and numbers.",
      "Don't return to cream paper, serif display type or stamp-red accents.",
      "Don't stack a second shadow inside a card or add a shadow to dark-mode stock.",
      "Don't round rectangular stock into pills; full rounds are for chips, avatars, circular buttons, toggles and person pills."
    ]
  }
}